    "content": {
     "content_type": "text",
     "parts": [
      "Likely questions and where you're exposed:\n\n**1. \"Who pays?\"** (weak spot)\nResearchers individually? Labs? Universities? Have a crisp first answer even if it's a hypothesis: e.g., *\"PhD students and postdocs pay $15–20/month individually first; lab plans later.\"* Show you know university procurement is slow.\n\n**2. \"Why now?\"**\nPeople's research thinking is now scattered across AI chats (ChatGPT, Claude), PDFs and notes. Nobody owns provenance across them.\n\n**3. \"Retention?\"** (weak spot: no data yet)\nSay what you'll measure in pilots: weekly active use, # of notes created that cite an imported source, return after 2 weeks. Name the pilots and dates.\n\n**4. \"Why you two?\"**\nYou: HCI PhD, built research tools, lived the problem. Hudson: [his strengths]. Keep it to two sentences each.\n\n**5. \"What's the wedge vs. Notion/Obsidian + AI?\"**\nThe import + provenance trail: \"where did this thought come from,\" across sources they already use.\n\n**6. \"Competition?\"**\nDon't say \"none.\" Name 3 and say what they don't do.\n\n**7. \"How much are you raising, on what terms?\"**\nKnow your answer (pre-seed SAFE, amount, cap or \"setting terms with lead\").\n\nHave one concrete demo moment ready: an idea in a note → click → the Claude chat and the PDF it came from."
     ]
    },
